---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Advertising Policy | AI Tool Hub" 
  description="How AI Tool Hub handles advertising, sponsored content, affiliate links, and partnerships. Clear disclosure on how to distinguish editorial from sponsored content."
  keywords="advertising policy, sponsored content, affiliate disclosure, AI Tool Hub ads"
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <span>Advertising Policy</span></nav>
    <header class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Transparency</span>
      <h1>Advertising &amp; Sponsorship Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">We believe readers deserve to know exactly who is paying for the content they consume. This page explains every form of advertising and sponsorship on AI Tool Hub, how we mark it, and how you can tell the difference between editorial and paid content.</p>
      <p class="lede-sub">Last updated: July 28, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Types of Advertising We Accept</h2>
      <p>AI Tool Hub uses the following forms of advertising and monetization. Each type is clearly labeled and visually distinct from editorial content.</p>

      <h3>1. Display Advertising (Google AdSense)</h3>
      <p>We serve contextual display ads through Google AdSense. These ads appear in three locations:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Top banner</strong> — above the fold on long-form article pages</li>
        <li><strong>Inline ads</strong> — within the body of long articles, between content sections</li>
        <li><strong>Sidebar ads</strong> — on the home page and category index pages</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Google AdSense ads are algorithmically served based on page content and user behavior. We do not choose which specific ads appear, we do not have direct relationships with the advertisers, and we do not receive higher payments for specific placements. AdSense ads do not influence our editorial content, rankings, or reviews in any way. You can block these ads using any standard ad blocker — the site will continue to function normally.</p>

      <h3>2. Affiliate Links</h3>
      <p>Some links on AI Tool Hub are affiliate links. When you click an affiliate link and make a purchase from the linked website, we may earn a small commission — at no additional cost to you.</p>
      <p><strong>How affiliate links are marked:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Affiliate links carry a visible "Affiliate" tag near the link</li>
        <li>The HTML includes the <code>rel="sponsored"</code> attribute for search engine compliance</li>
        <li>Affiliate relationships are disclosed on this page and in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>How affiliate links affect our content:</strong> They do not. We do not rank tools higher because we have an affiliate relationship, we do not write more favorable reviews for affiliate partners, and we do not accept exclusive affiliate deals that would create a financial incentive to favor one tool over another. If a better non-affiliate tool exists, we recommend it.</p>

      <h3>3. Sponsored Content</h3>
      <p>We occasionally publish sponsored content — articles, tutorials, or roundups that are paid for by a third party. Sponsored content is always clearly labeled and visually distinct from editorial content.</p>
      <p><strong>How sponsored content is marked:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>A "Sponsored" or "Partner Content" label at the top of the page</li>
        <li>Different background color or border treatment to visually separate from editorial</li>
        <li>Disclosure in the byline area identifying the sponsor</li>
        <li>"Sponsored" tag in index pages, category listings, and search results</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We only accept sponsored content that meets our editorial standards. Sponsored tutorials are written by our editorial team (not the sponsor), fact-checked, and must provide genuine value to readers. We never publish sponsored reviews of new tools — if a tool is worth reviewing, we review it for free.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How to Distinguish Editorial from Sponsored Content</h2>
      <p>We make it easy to tell what is editorial and what is paid. Here are the visual and contextual cues:</p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Characteristic</th>
            <th>Editorial Content</th>
            <th>Sponsored Content</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Label</strong></td>
            <td>No sponsor label; may show "Review" or "Guide" tag</td>
            <td>"Sponsored" or "Partner Content" label at the top</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Author</strong></td>
            <td>Named human reviewer with profile link</td>
            <td>"AI Tool Hub Editorial Team" (if written by us for a sponsor) or sponsor's named author with disclosure</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Background</strong></td>
            <td>Standard white/light background</td>
            <td>Slightly different background tint or border to signal different content type</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Links</strong></td>
            <td>Standard editorial links to tool pages, comparisons, and references</td>
            <td>May include trackable links labeled as sponsored; all affiliate links tagged</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Scoring</strong></td>
            <td>Contains our 5-dimension score and breakdown</td>
            <td>Never includes our review score — sponsored content is not a review</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>If you are ever unsure whether a piece of content is editorial or sponsored, look for the label at the top of the page. If there is no "Sponsored" label, it is editorial content. You can also check the URL: sponsored content routes through a dedicated path structure that differs from standard editorial URLs.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What We Will Never Do</h2>
      <p>Regardless of how much money is offered, we will never:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accept payment to change a review score.</strong> Scores are determined by our testing and rubric, not by sponsors.</li>
        <li><strong>Accept payment to rank a tool higher.</strong> Rankings in our directory are determined by our editorial judgment, not by advertising spend.</li>
        <li><strong>Accept payment to remove a negative review.</strong> If a tool has problems, we say so — and no amount of money changes that.</li>
        <li><strong>Disguise sponsored content as editorial.</strong> All sponsored content is clearly labeled. We never attempt to make paid content look like independent editorial.</li>
        <li><strong>Accept exclusive affiliate deals.</strong> We will not enter into agreements that require us to exclusively promote one tool in a category, regardless of whether better alternatives exist.</li>
        <li><strong>Sell user data for advertising.</strong> We do not collect user data for advertising purposes beyond standard server logs, and we do not sell or share any user data.</li>
        <li><strong>Run deceptive ad formats.</strong> No pop-unders, no forced redirects, no "Your computer is infected" scareware ads, no fake download buttons. Every ad on our site is clearly an ad.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Affiliate and Membership Relationship Disclosure</h2>
      <p>We maintain the following types of commercial relationships. All are disclosed here and on the relevant content pages.</p>

      <h3>Affiliate Partnerships</h3>
      <p>We participate in affiliate programs with select AI tool providers. As of the publication date, our affiliate relationships are limited and clearly documented. Current status: affiliate links are <strong>not yet active</strong> on the site. When they launch, each affiliate partner will be listed here with the nature of the relationship.</p>

      <h3>Tool Subscription Costs</h3>
      <p>To maintain editorial independence, we purchase our own subscriptions to the tools we test (ChatGPT Plus, Claude Pro, Midjourney, and others). We do not accept free vendor-provided accounts for review purposes. This costs us approximately $600/month in tool subscriptions. We disclose this because we believe readers should know that we have a financial stake in honest reviews — we are paying to use these tools, just like you would.</p>

      <h3>No Ownership Relationships</h3>
      <p>AI Tool Hub has no ownership stake in any AI tool company we review. No AI tool company has an ownership stake in AI Tool Hub. We are independently operated with no parent company or corporate affiliation that would create a conflict of interest.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How Advertising Revenue Is Used</h2>
      <p>All advertising revenue is used to support the operation of AI Tool Hub:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Paying for AI tool subscriptions used in testing (~$600/month)</li>
        <li>Compensating our editorial team for their time and expertise</li>
        <li>Hosting, infrastructure, and development costs</li>
        <li>Legal and compliance expenses</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not have investors, we are not venture-funded, and we are not pursuing growth at all costs. Our goal is to build a sustainable, editorially independent publication. If advertising revenue covers our costs, we continue. If it does not, we adjust the model — but we will never compromise our editorial independence for revenue.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact and Questions</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about our advertising practices, want to report a misleading ad, or are interested in advertising on AI Tool Hub:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Advertising inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@thebestaitoolsreview.com">contact@thebestaitoolsreview.com</a> (subject: "Advertising inquiry")</li>
        <li><strong>Report a misleading ad:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@thebestaitoolsreview.com">contact@thebestaitoolsreview.com</a> (subject: "Ad report")</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate partnership inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@thebestaitoolsreview.com">contact@thebestaitoolsreview.com</a> (subject: "Affiliate partnership")</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We respond to all inquiries within 5 business days. For detailed information about advertising options and rates, see our <a href="/advertise/">Advertise page</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
